The default pin includes completion_ordering.patch, a narrow backport of:
https://github.com/dougbinks/enkiTS/commit/845b837b6a5bb6f0d36d0e594610ba4dad0b81e1
https://github.com/dougbinks/enkiTS/commit/d1752d0898f4b1aa64a60944aaa9f6bf4b7ebfa4
Upstream report: https://github.com/dougbinks/enkiTS/issues/91
Only ten atomic read-modify-write memory orders change. The scheduling
algorithm and blocking semaphore behavior remain those of the pinned version.

Custom IR_ENKITS_GIT_REF revisions are not patched; their owner must include
these completion-ordering fixes. Custom revision source, binary, and population
directories are isolated by revision hash so Git cannot carry default patches
across a revision switch. The default pin is checked on every
configure, including already populated and disconnected dependency trees.

